A||||4||Greg Piet||Bypassing the throttle body heater||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||12-01-2000||12:38 PM||||Talking with some of my fellow racing competitors, we were discussing some of the "little" tricks some people do to get that extra fraction of a horsepower.  It was mentioned to me that some people bypass the coolant lines that run into the throttle body to suck in air that is just a little bit colder.  <P>Are there any adverse effects that may arise in a warm climate.  I realize this is not a good idea in cold weather regions.||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||12-01-2000||12:47 PM||||no problems at all.. just easy; free hp.. you'll need about 8" of 5/16" heater/fuel line. at the coolant inlet on the passengerside of the motor you'll see 2 small hoses that feed the hard lines under the intake.. undo these and bypass them from the block line to the block line.. NOT from the tb to tb.. that'd just squirt crap all over.. in EXTREME conditions you can ice over the TB butterfly. my cars have been like that for over 2 years and i've never had a problem (in Atlanta).. and one is in the snow now and still NO problems(Sioux Falls, SD).. (well the tires suck in the snow.. but thats not TB related) GT Bastard drives it now. BlackGT (in Atlanta too)(i did his too) also has had no problems. <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||12-01-2000||06:47 PM||||cool beans!<BR>Since I am upgrading to a higher class next season, I want to give myself every little bit of help within the rulebook, especially since I do not have the funds to install a $1000 racing suspension kit.<P>Anyone wanna sponsor me???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||12-02-2000||11:57 PM||||1FST2M6:<P>   Could you send me a picture or two of what you are talking about?  I'd really appreciate it.<P>c311t@yahoo.com||||reg||1
Z||000004||HYPTNOTiSE||12-03-2000||02:55 AM||||When i re-did mine guys, i took the thermostat housing and welded the ports shut on it.  It's a little bit cleaner look, also i ditched the coolant pipes that run to the TB for a cleaner look, and i got some metric bolts, can't remember the size right now, they fit the fittings on the TB. Not really necessary but it gives it a cleaner finished look. I should take pictures of the clean look, so everyone can take a look at the clean look.  Sorry for getting stupid here, it's just that it's 2:50 and i'm really really tired.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
